{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1221579-returning-weapon-how-to-do-it","id":1221579,"title":"Returning Weapon: how to do it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-23T17:28:36-07:00","id":1221579,"title":"Returning Weapon: how to do it?","content":"In both the original myths and the comics, when Thor hurls Mj\u00f6lnir, the hammer will then return to his hand. How would you do that in Mage? I'm thinking an Enhanced item (since the spell(s)) needed would be of Indefinite duration), but I'm not sure of the spells. I'm currently thinking Forces 3 or 4 to make it come back, and Space 1 to guide it to the thrower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T18:31:33-07:00","id":1221586,"title":"","content":"You can do it lots of ways, Forces for telekinetic returning, Space for Teleporting, Fate to have it destined to return to you, you could animate its spirit or haunt it with a ghost to bring it back to you, you could even imbue it with Time so that it casts Shifting Sands on what it hits sending the target back to just before you struck it so the weapon will still/always have been in your hand.<br /> <br /> If you go the Forces route you don\u2019t need Space to guide it except in exceptional circumstances of navigation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T20:40:09-07:00","id":1221608,"title":"","content":"Potency 2, Indefinite duration Co-Location spell, tagged to your hammer, and the area directly in front of the palm of your hand.<br /> Assuming that you'd be able to 'perceive' the overlap, (which wouldn't be unreasonable, for a Mage used to practicing with it), then you could draw your weapon back across with a Reflexive action.<br /> <br /> At least, that's how I'd do it.<br /> I do love Co-Locations so.<br /> <br /> *edit*<br /> Of course, it'd be tagged to one person, unless you tagged a glove or something.<br /> And it's probably best to 'Key' it, so people can't get you using it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":". 05-23-2018, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T02:04:51-07:00","id":1221632,"title":"","content":"I believe there is or at least was a fate spell that made an item return to the owner. Bad Penny? Monkey's paw? I forget which.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T04:46:46-07:00","id":1221656,"title":"","content":"As pointed out, it all depends on <u>how</u> you want it to return. For a Comic/Movie Mjolnir, a Delayed Forces telekinetic effect is fine. (Though @HerbertIsTheBestBert's suggestion of a Keyed, Co-Locations spell seems like the most useful. You could even leave it at home, then &quot;draw&quot; it when you want.)<br /> <br /> And it might actually work better as Imbued, since it seems to be a triggered effect as opposed to passive-permanent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-24-2018, 07:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T07:13:59-07:00","id":1221695,"title":"","content":"I was thinking in terms of myth/comic/movie returning, yes. The problem with imbuing it is that conditional spells only happen once. You throw it, it returns. Once. Conditional Duration is very clear on this point: one the spell goes off, it ends. That's the sticking point: how to make it come back more than once. Of course, I might well be grossly misunderstanding something about either Imbue Item, Conditional Duration, or their interaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 05-24-2018, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T07:40:47-07:00","id":1221703,"title":"","content":"That sounds like it'd just be an imbued item or persistent effect (persistent telekinesis or co-location)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T07:49:42-07:00","id":1221706,"title":"","content":"Co-Location on the hammer and your hand (maybe with a Reach to stabilise the hand around the hammer's handle so you don't have to look down and adjust your grip?) keyed to the hammer (so only the hammer can pass through) could work. Either persistent so you could always draw the hammer from wherever, or set to be cast when the hammer is thrown so that you have a turn or two to get it back. That way you could lend it to other people, as well as lose the direct connection (but not necessarily the sympathetic connection if you've used the hammer for a while or were its creator) if you for some reason have to leave it behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T13:39:03-07:00","id":1221828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1221579-returning-weapon-how-to-do-it?p=1221695#post1221695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking in terms of myth/comic/movie returning, yes. The problem with imbuing it is that conditional spells only happen once. You throw it, it returns. Once. Conditional Duration is very clear on this point: one the spell goes off, it ends. That's the sticking point: how to make it come back more than once. Of course, I might well be grossly misunderstanding something about either Imbue Item, Conditional Duration, or their interaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Imbue, it would work like this:<br /> 1. I want the hammer to return, so I activate the Imbued effect for 1 Mana.<br /> 2. Delayed timer starts.<br /> 3. I throw the hammer.<br /> 4. Timer expires, and the Forces spell telekinetically returns the hammer to my hand.<br /> 5. Repeat as desired, unless the Imbued item runs out of Mana.<br /> <br /> The Imbuement is permanent. The spells it triggers are treated as normal spells (excepting Spell Control). To have the hammer return multiple times, activate the Imbued item multiple time.<br /> <br /> EDIT: For Fate instead of Time, you could use Conditional Duration, keyed to &quot;the thrown hammer hitting its target&quot;. You'd still want it Imbued, otherwise the Condition would only trigger once, then the hammer would be stuck to your hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-24-2018, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}